{
  "about": "The engines.vizi grammar: at most one leading prefix, exactly '>=', '^' or '~'; then MAJOR, MAJOR.MINOR or MAJOR.x, MAJOR and MINOR each one or more ASCII digits (leading zeros allowed, so '01.0' is 1.0); 'MAJOR' and 'MAJOR.x' read as minor 0. No whitespace anywhere (nothing is trimmed), no sign, no underscore, no other digit characters, no third component, no '*' or 'X'. Each component is at most 4294967295; a larger one is not a version, never wrapped or clamped. Anything else is refused as an invalid manifest before any other check: a component with a minus sign ('-1.0', '1.-1') as 'engines.vizi '...' has a negative component', and the rest as 'engines.vizi '...' is not a version'. Read by the Go, Rust and Java parsers' tests and by scripts/check_manifest_fixtures.py; expected.kind is 'accepted', 'engines_incompatible' (a version this protocol cannot run, the message exactly expected.message) or 'invalid' (the message contains expected.message).",
  "protocol": "1.0",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "major.minor is accepted",
      "json": {"manifest_version": 1, "id": "org.example.grammar", "name": "Grammar", "version": "1", "engines": {"vizi": "1.0"}, "entry": {"command": ["python3"]}},
      "expected": {"kind": "accepted"}
    },
    {
      "name": "a '>=' prefix is accepted",
      "json": {"manifest_version": 1, "id": "org.example.grammar", "name": "Grammar", "version": "1", "engines": {"vizi": ">=1.0"}, "entry": {"command": ["python3"]}},
      "expected": {"kind": "accepted"}
    },
    {
      "name": "a '^' prefix is accepted",
      "json": {"manifest_version": 1, "id": "org.example.grammar", "name": "Grammar", "version": "1", "engines": {"vizi": "^1.0"}, "entry": {"command": ["python3"]}},
      "expected": {"kind": "accepted"}
    },
    {
      "name": "a '~' prefix is accepted",
